    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a lineup anchored by the high-ceiling potential of **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56) and **Kyle Tucker** (74.44). **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefits from a favorable matchup against Holmes, where his dynamic platoon advantage and a move up to the #2 spot provide a significant boost to his base projection. Meanwhile, **Kyle Tucker** faces a vulnerable arm in Gasser; despite the modest park factor, his elite skill set against Gasser\u2019s 5.63 xERA makes him an essential start. **Andy Pages** (69.18) also finds himself in a prime position, taking advantage of the same soft matchup against Gasser to secure his place as one of our most reliable options today.\n\nWe are navigating a few situational challenges, most notably the benching of **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (50.94), who falls into the marginal category due to a brutal matchup against the elite Skenes (2.96 xERA). His -19% SP skill penalty essentially neutralized his offensive upside. **Nolan Schanuel** (44.77) serves as our most difficult omission, falling just short of the starting rotation. While he possesses a strong base projection, he was outperformed by the efficiency scores of **Sam Antonacci** (62.33) and **Josh Jung** (63.26), both of whom benefit from favorable matchups against Houser and Ure\u00f1a. \n\nThe injury report and weather conditions demand disciplined roster management today. We are tracking a major disruption with **Gunnar Henderson**, who is sidelined due to a rainout/postponement, further thinning our depth alongside the continuing absences of **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg** on the IL. As we look at the remainder of the bench\u2014which includes **Jacob Wilson**, **Drake Baldwin**, **Jorge Polanco**, **Josh Lowe**, **Heliot Ramos**, **Coby Mayo**, **Brayan Rocchio**, and **Gage Workman**\u2014we will remain vigilant for any late-breaking lineup changes that might necessitate a pivot to keep our 5x5 categories competitive.",
